2026-11-07T06:51:33.8003270Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-07T06:51:33.8047590Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-07T06:51:33.8049330Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-07T06:51:33.8050190Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-07T06:51:33.8050800Z 
2026-11-07T06:51:33.8054630Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-07T06:51:33.8055120Z 
2026-11-07T06:51:33.8055530Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-07T06:51:33.8058120Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-07T06:51:33.8058800Z 
2026-11-07T06:51:33.8059050Z If you would like to
2026-11-07T06:51:33.8059980Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-07T06:51:33.8060280Z 
2026-11-07T06:51:33.8060500Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-07T06:51:33.8060860Z   $ sh ./install-nix
